       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen has no therapeutic use. For a 70 kg adult it is in the range that causes acute liver injury and can be fatal. Normal liver function doesn't protect against that, and a dose like this can easily be given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Examples are 1000 mg PO three times daily or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. I'll enter whichever you choose right away.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 5000 was meant to be 500 or 1000, tell me the intended dose.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you have a specific clinical reason for an unusual regimen, a pharmacist or attending can review it. The order would then go through your hospital's override process rather than my standard entry.\n\nWhat would you like to do?"
      }
